  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_015 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy / 0.6847 F1. The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer as the top-performing architecture, with weighted fusion at 0.7250 vs avgpool at 0.7062. The one untested cell in this top combination is concat fusion with transformer aggregation (config_033). While weighted has outperformed concat in prior comparisons (pca_n2000: 0.6352 vs 0.6287; scvi_n200 avgpool: 0.7062 vs untested), the interaction between transformer aggregation and concat fusion is unknown—concat preserves full representation and may complement transformer's attention-based aggregation differently than weighted does. This experiment directly tests whether a small architectural tweak to the best config can push accuracy above 0.7250. Expected cost is comparable to config_015 (~3.5–3.6 GPU hours) since the architecture is identical except for the fusion method (concat is marginally cheaper than weighted as it avoids learning per-modality weights). With 2 experiments remaining after this, confirming or ruling out concat fusion here preserves the final experiment for a more exploratory direction if needed."
}

